   "date": "2017-07-31T04:38:46Z",
   "subject": "Latent trait variance-covariance matrix became non-positive definite.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Dr. Chalmers,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I used IRTPRO to run some IRT models but now I am trying to\r\nuse MIRT. <span style=\"font-family:Wingdings\"><span>:) <br></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I tried to run this IRT model with two correlated\r\ndimensions, but I am getting the following error:</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; model &lt;- mirt.model(&#39;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">+ <span>               </span>F1 =\r\n1,2,5,6,9,10,13,14,15,19,21,22,25,26,29,30,34,36,37,38</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">+ <span>              </span><span> </span>F2 =\r\n3,4,7,8,11,12,16,17,18,20,23,24,27,28,31,32,33,35,39,40</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">+ <span>                    </span>COV = F1*F2&#39;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; bidim_EM &lt;- mirt(d,\r\nmodel, method = &#39;EM&#39;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">Iteration: 55, Log-Lik:\r\n-14744.848, Max-Change: 0.03093</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Warning message:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Latent trait\r\nvariance-covariance matrix became non-positive definite.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am able to run this model using MHRM but not using EM. Do\r\nyou have any suggestions of what I can do to solve this problem?</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you so much for any guidance,</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Ane</p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
